<sheet>
<plain>
<text x="304.8" y="27.94" size="2.54" layer="91">D-BS-8i-0-11 Teletype Receivers</text>
<text x="99.06" y="185.42" size="1.778" layer="94">Note: The backplane, as drawn, is configured for:</text>
<text x="106.68" y="177.8" size="1.778" layer="94">8 bit characters</text>
<text x="106.68" y="175.26" size="1.778" layer="94">2 stop bits</text>
<text x="106.68" y="180.34" size="1.778" layer="94">03 device code</text>
<text x="99.06" y="170.18" size="1.778" layer="94">Backplane wiring changes would be needed to change these settings.</text>
<text x="99.06" y="167.64" size="1.778" layer="94">This may be an issue for non-wire-wrap-backplanes.</text>
<text x="99.06" y="198.12" size="1.778" layer="94">Teletype Receiver</text>
</plain>
